  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Generated FLINT resources now implement canonical gcd for ZZ[x] and QQ[x] through two ordinary declarations and the existing resource ABI, with no native-compiler or handwritten N-API changes. PolynomialElement.gcd selects one resource-to-resource call on Node and retains a small ordinary-Python Euclidean oracle for portable hosts. Tests cover Sage-compatible zero, constant, content, sign, and monic normalization; deterministic varied inputs; 8193-bit coefficient skew; closed and unsealed handles; native-disabled execution; forced portable storage; no compatibility materialization; and sanitizer-backed lifecycle cleanup. The focused generated-resource benchmark measures degree-4000 ZZ at 74.92 ms with a 4097-bit coefficient and degree-2000 QQ at 12.82 ms; the central small-coefficient performance ratchet measures 0.32 ms and 0.22 ms respectively.",
    "risks": [
      "The correct portable ZZ fallback computes a monic gcd over QQ and clears denominators, so coefficient swell can make it much slower than FLINT on large inputs; Node always selects the generated FLINT resource operation.",
      "Exact polynomial resources still declare wasm=False; browser execution uses the tested ordinary-Python packed fallback until generated Wasm resource ownership is implemented."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Use the same declaration-only pattern for resultant, extended gcd, and squarefree decomposition when those public operations are added.",
      "Enable the existing exact-polynomial resource ABI for Wasm so browser hosts can select FLINT instead of the portable oracle."
    ]
  }
